#WRITES
#AUTO 52
#NEEDED 0
# backlight-duty — read the live state of both backlight PWM channels.
#
# display-recon (prio 51) reports whether the VOP2 is scanning pixels; this
# reads the other half of "is the screen lit": the backlight. The two
# pwm-backlights are PWM3 (0xFE700000) channel 0 for screen 0 and the next
# channel (0xFE700010) for screen 1, both 40 kHz (per the device tree). Reading
# a PWM register while its pclk is gated hangs the bus, so SAVE the PWM3 clock
# gate, ungate it, read, and RESTORE to as-found (issue 110o).
#
# Per-channel register block (each channel is 0x10 apart), from the PWM1
# bring-up in 003-pwm.c / pwm-bringup.probe (RK3568 TRM Part1 Ch15):
#   +0x00 CNT (RO)   +0x04 PERIOD_HPR   +0x08 DUTY_LPR   +0x0C CTRL (bit0 pwm_en)
# Brightness = DUTY / PERIOD. CTRL bit0 set = the channel is driving; if a
# channel reads pwm_en=0 (or CTRL 0x0), that backlight is not being driven.
#
# Clock gate: CRU_CLKGATE_CON32 @ 0xFDD20380 — bit0 pclk_pwm3, bit1 clk_pwm3
# (0 = on). Masked ungate of bits 0,1 = 0x00030000 (TRM Part1 CRU, confirmed).

SAVE 0xFDD20380
LOG ungate PWM3 pclk+clk (CLKGATE_CON32 bits 0,1 -> 0) so its registers read
W 0xFDD20380 0x00030000
DELAY 10000

LOG screen0 backlight (pwm@0xFE700000): PERIOD, DUTY, CTRL (bit0 = enabled)
R 0xFE700004
R 0xFE700008
R 0xFE70000C
LOG screen1 backlight (pwm@0xFE700010): PERIOD, DUTY, CTRL (bit0 = enabled)
R 0xFE700014
R 0xFE700018
R 0xFE70001C

LOG restore PWM3 clock gate to as-found
RESTORE 0xFDD20380 0x0003

LOG backlight-duty complete: DUTY/PERIOD is the brightness fraction; CTRL bit0
LOG   clear or CTRL=0x0 means that screen's backlight PWM is not running
